  </aside>
</div></section>
<section class="section section--cream"><div class="wrap">
  <div class="section-head reveal" style="justify-content:center;text-align:center"><div><p class="eyebrow">Questions</p><h2>Artist&#x27;s garden FAQs</h2></div></div>
  <div class="faq"><details class="reveal"><summary>What is atmospheric planting?</summary><div class="answer"><p>Planting designed for mood rather than display: a limited colour palette, soft and see-through plants, grasses for movement and plants that look good as they fade.</p></div></details><details class="reveal"><summary>Can you design a garden around an existing studio?</summary><div class="answer"><p>Yes. We look at the views from the studio, the light and the practical needs of the work, and plan the garden around them.</p></div></details><details class="reveal"><summary>Will an artist&#x27;s garden need a lot of maintenance?</summary><div class="answer"><p>Naturalistic planting is usually less work than formal bedding: one big cut-back in late winter and occasional editing of self-seeders.</p></div></details></div>
</div></section>
